    exploradorTitulo: "Data explorer for a single stock",
    exploradorDesc: "Queries ALL the data modules Yahoo Finance offers for a stock in the index and shows what each one returns — not just the fields the application currently uses (P/E, EPS, price-to-book, dividend and analyst consensus), but everything available: balance sheet, income statement, annual and quarterly cash flows, key statistics, earnings calendar, institutional holdings, recommendation history and more. It's a reconnaissance tool, to see what information actually exists before deciding whether it's worth building something with it. Each module is queried separately: availability varies a lot by stock and market, so one that doesn't exist is flagged as unavailable without preventing the others from coming through.",
    exploradorEtiquetaTicker: "Stock to explore:",
    exploradorBoton: "Explore all data",
    exploradorBotonCargando: "Querying all modules (may take a while)...",
    exploradorResumen: (disponibles, total) => `${disponibles} of ${total} modules returned data for this stock.`,
    exploradorDatosCotizacion: "Quote data",
    exploradorModulosConDatos: "Modules with data (sorted by amount of information):",
    exploradorModulosSinDatos: "Modules with no data for this stock:",
